      justification: "R106.SHELL-003 (paideia-os/shell#42) case overflow: cap=1 forces tk_overflow at src/tokenizer.pdx:218-219 on the second word start. The first word ('a' at (0,1)) is already emitted -- the SUT does not roll back partial output. Asserts both the error sentinel AND that the first token record is (0,1), which pins the exact SUT behaviour a caller should expect: 'cap tokens are written, then OVERFLOW is returned; no undo'.",
